### Personal Sandbox Secrets

The thread owner saved these secrets for their private threads. Each environment variable holds only a placeholder; the sandbox proxy replaces the named header with the real value on requests to the listed hosts, so ordinary SDKs and CLIs work unchanged. The real values are never in the sandbox, so do not print, copy, or try to recover them, and do not send the variable to other hosts.

{% for secret in secrets %}
- `{{ secret.name }}`: `{{ secret.header_name }}` header on `{{ secret.hosts | join("`, `") }}`
{% endfor %}

If a needed credential is missing, ask the owner to add it under Settings → Connections → Sandbox secrets; it applies from the next message.
